@startuml client_send_queue_send_wait_reply_activity
title ClientSendQueue - sending and waiting for a reply

start
:SendWaitReply(message, reply);
if (message.size() > max_send_size_?) then (yes)
    :Return EMSGSIZE;
    stop
else (no)
    :Message size is admissible;
endif
if (!lifetime_.IsAccepting()?) then (yes)
    :Return EINVAL;
    stop
else (no)
    :Prepare result and NonAllocatingFuture;
endif
:Create completion callback capturing reply and future;
note right
    On error, store the error and mark the future ready.
    An oversized reply stores EMSGSIZE.
    Otherwise copy the reply into the caller's buffer,
    store its trimmed span, and mark the future ready.
end note
:Lock lifetime_.mutex_ and create Operation;
if (Operation rejected admission?) then (yes)
    :End rejected operation scope and unlock;
    :Return EINVAL;
    stop
else (no)
    :Retain the admitted operation;
endif
if (reply slot engaged?) then (yes)
    :TryQueue(message, move(completion callback));
    if (Queue admission failed?) then (yes)
        :End Operation scope and unlock;
        :Return ENOBUFS;
        stop
    else (no)
        :Queued request admitted with its completion callback;
    endif
else (direct)
    :Reserve completion and identify this sender;
    :SendTransport(operation, REQUEST, message);
    if (Transport failed and this sender still owns completion?) then (yes)
        :Reset the slot and sender owner;
        :ArmIfNeeded();
        :End Operation scope and unlock;
        :Return the transport error;
        stop
    else (no)
        :Keep successful or already-transferred completion;
    endif
endif
:Unlock lifetime_.mutex_;
:future.Wait(): wait for its ready predicate;
:Relock lifetime_.mutex_;
:End Operation scope and unlock;
:Return the completion result;
stop

legend
    Callback-thread rejection belongs to the facade, not this helper.
    A free reply slot selects direct transport independently of config modes.
    Stop cancellation wakes the future; no application reply is required.
    The operation remains registered through completion and termination.
    No overall reply deadline is imposed here.
endlegend

@enduml